id pub-id-type="pmid">12517711</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Pazour, G.J., B.L. Dickert, and G.B. Witman. <year>1999</year>. The DHC1b (DHC2) isoform of cytoplasmic dynein is required for flagellar assembly. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>144</volume>:<fpage>473</fpage>&#x02013;481.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9971742</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Peckol, E.L., J.A. Zallen, J.C. Yarrow, and C.I. Bargmann. <year>1999</year>. Sensory activity affects sensory axon development in <source>C. elegans. Development.</source> <volume>126</volume>:<fpage>1891</fpage>&#x02013;1902.</citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Perkins, L.A., E.M. Hedgecock, J.N. Thomson, and J.G. Culotti. <year>1986</year>. Mutant sensory cilia in the nematode <source>Caenorhabditis elegans. Dev. Biol.</source> <volume>117</volume>:<fpage>456</fpage>&#x02013;487.</citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Porter, M.E., R. Bower, J.A. Knott, P. Byrd, and W. Dentler. <year>1999</year>. Cytoplasmic dynein heavy chain 1b is required for flagellar assembly in <source>Chlamydomonas. Mol. Biol. Cell.</source> <volume>10</volume>:<fpage>693</fpage>&#x02013;712.</citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Reese, T.S. <year>1965</year>. Olfactory cilia in the frog. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>25</volume>:<fpage>209</fpage>&#x02013;230.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5840799</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Rosenbaum, J.L., and G.B. Witman. <year>2002</year>. Intraflagellar transport. <source>Nat. Rev. Mol. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>3</volume>:<fpage>813</fpage>&#x02013;825.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12415299</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Scholey, J.M. <year>2003</year>. Intraflagellar transport. <source>Annu. Rev. Cell Dev. Biol.</source> <volume>19</v